  #block(breakable: false)[
  === Complete Solutions

  #sol-item(1, "C", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    Nothing can be recorded until a transaction with a financial effect has been identified.
  ]

  #sol-item(2, "B", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    Prudence provides for known losses but never anticipates profit.
  ]
  ]

  #sol-item(3, "B", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    Realisation fixes the point of sale at delivery.
  ]

  #sol-item(4, "B", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    Assets = liabilities + capital = 270,000 + 430,000 = ₦700,000.
  ]

  #sol-item(5, "C", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    Cash falls and the liability falls by the same amount, so the equation holds.
  ]

  #sol-item(6, "D", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    Credits increase liabilities, income and capital.
  ]

  #sol-item(7, "B", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    Capital = liabilities... assets = liabilities + capital + profit − drawings.
  ]

  #sol-item(8, "C", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    The supplier accepts the return and reduces the buyer's account with a credit note.
  ]

  #sol-item(9, "B", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    Returns outwards records goods the firm sends back.
  ]

  #sol-item(10, "D", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    It records cash transactions and also serves as the cash account.
  ]

  #sol-item(11, "C", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    An asset carries a debit balance.
  ]

  #sol-item(12, "C", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    An error of principle touches both sides equally, so the totals still agree.
  ]

  #sol-item(13, "A", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    The credits are short by ₦48,000, so suspense is credited with that amount.
  ]

  #sol-item(14, "C", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    One account controls all the individual creditors.
  ]

  #sol-item(15, "D", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    Purchases = 180,000 − 150,000 + 620,000 + 20,000 = ₦670,000.
  ]

  #sol-item(16, "B", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    480,000 − 20,000 + 60,000 = ₦520,000.
  ]

  #sol-item(17, "C", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    The bank has already paid it, so the firm must record it.
  ]

  #sol-item(18, "B", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    Money owed to the bank is a credit balance in the firm's cash book.
  ]

  #sol-item(19, "A", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    The firm cannot alter the bank's record, so it asks the bank to correct it.
  ]

  #sol-item(20, "C", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    Cost is 500,000 ÷ 1.25 = ₦400,000, so the gross profit is ₦100,000.
  ]

  #sol-item(21, "C", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    Gross profit 270,000 ÷ 900,000 = 30%.
  ]

  #sol-item(22, "A", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    Cost 100, profit 20, price 120; margin = 20/120 = 16.7%.
  ]

  #sol-item(23, "B", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    Six months of cover belongs to this year: 240,000 × 6/12 = ₦120,000.
  ]

  #sol-item(24, "C", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    Year one 200,000 leaves 1,800,000; year two is 10% of that = ₦180,000.
  ]

  #sol-item(25, "A", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    New provision 30,000 less existing 20,000 = ₦10,000.
  ]

  #sol-item(26, "B", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    It is the total written off to date, netted against the cost of the asset.
  ]

  #sol-item(27, "C", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    450,000 − 180,000 = ₦270,000.
  ]

  #sol-item(28, "B", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    180,000 ÷ 1,200,000 = 15%.
  ]

  #sol-item(29, "D", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    The expense is missing from the profit calculation and an asset has been invented.
  ]

  #sol-item(30, "D", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    Both sides of the sale are missing, so the trial balance agrees while the profit is understated.
  ]

  #sol-item(31, "A", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    Only one side of the double entry was posted, so the totals differ.
  ]

  #sol-item(32, "D", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    Both sides are equally wrong, so the trial balance agrees but purchases and creditors are overstated by ₦63,000.
  ]

  #sol-item(33, "A", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    A difference divisible by nine suggests reversed digits.
  ]

  #sol-item(34, "D", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    Income was recorded too low, so profit is too low.
  ]

  #sol-item(35, "C", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    Sleeping describes management, not liability.
  ]

  #sol-item(36, "B", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    The capital account holds the permanent stake; the current account holds the running balance of profit and drawings.
  ]

  #sol-item(37, "D", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    Drawings reduce what the firm owes the partner.
  ]

  #sol-item(38, "A", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    The shareholder owns a part of the company; the debenture holder lends to it.
  ]

  #sol-item(39, "D", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    Dividend rates are quoted on nominal value, which is why a 10% share of ₦1 pays 10 kobo.
  ]

  #sol-item(40, "D", dense: true, pad: 14.22pt)[
    The club owes the member a period of membership, so the money is a liability until earned.
  ]

